WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.985
Two islands, two very different landscapes.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:08.420
Pitcairn is a dissected volcano of steep valleys and cliffs.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.229
The village, Adamstown, sits on a terrace high above Bounty Bay,

00:00:12.229 --> 00:00:15.085
reached by a road called the Hill of Difficulty.

00:00:15.085 --> 00:00:20.024
There is no natural harbour, so people and cargo land by longboat through the surf.

00:00:21.124 --> 00:00:26.023
Henderson is limestone throughout: a jagged, honeycombed plateau called makatea,

00:00:26.023 --> 00:00:28.839
under dense forest, edged by cliffs and caves.

00:00:28.839 --> 00:00:33.860
There are beaches only on the north and east coasts, and no permanent fresh water.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:39.623
From the sea, Henderson's raised reef shows as a line of grey limestone cliffs,

00:00:39.623 --> 00:00:41.984
with sandy beaches only in a few places.

00:00:43.084 --> 00:00:47.509
Oeno and Ducie are low rings of reef with lagoons and a few sandy islets,

00:00:47.509 --> 00:00:49.692
much like Funafuti, but uninhabited.

00:00:49.692 --> 00:00:54.602
Together the four islands show a volcanic island's whole life in one archipelago.
